Draws data using bound graphics state with an index buffer and instancing enabled.

You must not call this function before binding a graphics pipeline.

Note that the `first_vertex` and `first_instance` parameters are NOT compatible with built-in vertex/instance ID variables in shaders (for example, SV_VertexID); GPU APIs and shader languages do not define these built-in variables consistently, so if your shader depends on them, the only way to keep behavior consistent and portable is to always pass 0 for the correlating parameter in the draw calls.

=over

=item render_pass - SDL3::GPURenderPass object or undef. a render pass handle.

=item num_indices - unsigned integer. the number of indices to draw per instance.

=item num_instances - unsigned integer. the number of instances to draw.

=item first_index - unsigned integer. the starting index within the index buffer.

=item vertex_offset - integer. value added to vertex index before indexing into the vertex buffer.

=item first_instance - unsigned integer. the ID of the first instance to draw.

=back

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

