=head2 SDL_GPUTextureType

Specifies the type of a texture.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_TEXTURETYPE_2D = 0 - The texture is a 2-dimensional image.

=item SDL_GPU_TEXTURETYPE_2D_ARRAY = 1 - The texture is a 2-dimensional array image.

=item SDL_GPU_TEXTURETYPE_3D = 2 - The texture is a 3-dimensional image.

=item SDL_GPU_TEXTURETYPE_CUBE = 3 - The texture is a cube image.

=item SDL_GPU_TEXTURETYPE_CUBE_ARRAY = 4 - The texture is a cube array image.

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUSampleCount

Specifies the sample count of a texture.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_SAMPLECOUNT_1 = 0 - No multisampling.

=item SDL_GPU_SAMPLECOUNT_2 = 1 - MSAA 2x

=item SDL_GPU_SAMPLECOUNT_4 = 2 - MSAA 4x

=item SDL_GPU_SAMPLECOUNT_8 = 3 - MSAA 8x

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUCubeMapFace

Specifies the face of a cube map.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_CUBEMAPFACE_POSITIVEX = 0

=item SDL_GPU_CUBEMAPFACE_NEGATIVEX = 1

=item SDL_GPU_CUBEMAPFACE_POSITIVEY = 2

=item SDL_GPU_CUBEMAPFACE_NEGATIVEY = 3

=item SDL_GPU_CUBEMAPFACE_POSITIVEZ = 4

=item SDL_GPU_CUBEMAPFACE_NEGATIVEZ = 5

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUTransferBufferUsage

Specifies how a transfer buffer is intended to be used by the client.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_TRANSFERBUFFERUSAGE_UPLOAD = 0

=item SDL_GPU_TRANSFERBUFFERUSAGE_DOWNLOAD = 1

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUShaderStage

Specifies which stage a shader program corresponds to.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_SHADERSTAGE_VERTEX = 0

=item SDL_GPU_SHADERSTAGE_FRAGMENT = 1

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUVertexElementFormat

Specifies the format of a vertex attribute.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_INVALID = 0

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_INT = 1

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_INT2 = 2

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_INT3 = 3

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_INT4 = 4

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_UINT = 5

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_UINT2 = 6

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_UINT3 = 7

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_UINT4 = 8

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_FLOAT = 9

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_FLOAT2 = 10

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_FLOAT3 = 11

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_FLOAT4 = 12

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_BYTE2 = 13

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_BYTE4 = 14

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_UBYTE2 = 15

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_UBYTE4 = 16

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_BYTE2_NORM = 17

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_BYTE4_NORM = 18

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_UBYTE2_NORM = 19

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_UBYTE4_NORM = 20

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_SHORT2 = 21

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_SHORT4 = 22

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_USHORT2 = 23

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_USHORT4 = 24

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_SHORT2_NORM = 25

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_SHORT4_NORM = 26

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_USHORT2_NORM = 27

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_USHORT4_NORM = 28

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_HALF2 = 29

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXELEMENTFORMAT_HALF4 = 30

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUVertexInputRate

Specifies the rate at which vertex attributes are pulled from buffers.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXINPUTRATE_VERTEX = 0 - Attribute addressing is a function of the vertex index.

=item SDL_GPU_VERTEXINPUTRATE_INSTANCE = 1 - Attribute addressing is a function of the instance index.

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUFillMode

Specifies the fill mode of the graphics pipeline.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_FILLMODE_FILL = 0 - Polygons will be rendered via rasterization.

=item SDL_GPU_FILLMODE_LINE = 1 - Polygon edges will be drawn as line segments.

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUCullMode

Specifies the facing direction in which triangle faces will be culled.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_CULLMODE_NONE = 0 - No triangles are culled.

=item SDL_GPU_CULLMODE_FRONT = 1 - Front-facing triangles are culled.

=item SDL_GPU_CULLMODE_BACK = 2 - Back-facing triangles are culled.

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUFrontFace

Specifies the vertex winding that will cause a triangle to be determined to be front-facing.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_FRONTFACE_COUNTER_CLOCKWISE = 0 - A triangle with counter-clockwise vertex winding will be considered front-facing.

=item SDL_GPU_FRONTFACE_CLOCKWISE = 1 - A triangle with clockwise vertex winding will be considered front-facing.

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUCompareOp

Specifies a comparison operator for depth, stencil and sampler operations.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_COMPAREOP_INVALID = 0

=item SDL_GPU_COMPAREOP_NEVER = 1 - The comparison always evaluates false.

=item SDL_GPU_COMPAREOP_LESS = 2 - The comparison evaluates reference < test.

=item SDL_GPU_COMPAREOP_EQUAL = 3 - The comparison evaluates reference == test.

=item SDL_GPU_COMPAREOP_LESS_OR_EQUAL = 4 - The comparison evaluates reference < = test.

=item SDL_GPU_COMPAREOP_GREATER = 5 - The comparison evaluates reference > test.

=item SDL_GPU_COMPAREOP_NOT_EQUAL = 6 - The comparison evaluates reference != test.

=item SDL_GPU_COMPAREOP_GREATER_OR_EQUAL = 7 - The comparison evaluates reference >= test.

=item SDL_GPU_COMPAREOP_ALWAYS = 8 - The comparison always evaluates true.

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUStencilOp

Specifies what happens to a stored stencil value if stencil tests fail or pass.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_STENCILOP_INVALID = 0

=item SDL_GPU_STENCILOP_KEEP = 1 - Keeps the current value.

=item SDL_GPU_STENCILOP_ZERO = 2 - Sets the value to 0.

=item SDL_GPU_STENCILOP_REPLACE = 3 - Sets the value to reference.

=item SDL_GPU_STENCILOP_INCREMENT_AND_CLAMP = 4 - Increments the current value and clamps to the maximum value.

=item SDL_GPU_STENCILOP_DECREMENT_AND_CLAMP = 5 - Decrements the current value and clamps to 0.

=item SDL_GPU_STENCILOP_INVERT = 6 - Bitwise-inverts the current value.

=item SDL_GPU_STENCILOP_INCREMENT_AND_WRAP = 7 - Increments the current value and wraps back to 0.

=item SDL_GPU_STENCILOP_DECREMENT_AND_WRAP = 8 - Decrements the current value and wraps to the maximum value.

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUBlendOp

Specifies the operator to be used when pixels in a render target are blended with existing pixels in the texture.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDOP_INVALID = 0

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDOP_ADD = 1 - (source * source_factor) + (destination * destination_factor)

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDOP_SUBTRACT = 2 - (source * source_factor) - (destination * destination_factor)

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDOP_REVERSE_SUBTRACT = 3 - (destination * destination_factor) - (source * source_factor)

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDOP_MIN = 4 - min(source, destination)

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDOP_MAX = 5 - max(source, destination)

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUBlendFactor

Specifies a blending factor to be used when pixels in a render target are blended with existing pixels in the texture.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDFACTOR_INVALID = 0

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDFACTOR_ZERO = 1 - 0

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDFACTOR_ONE = 2 - 1

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDFACTOR_SRC_COLOR = 3 - source color

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDFACTOR_ONE_MINUS_SRC_COLOR = 4 - 1 - source color

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDFACTOR_DST_COLOR = 5 - destination color

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDFACTOR_ONE_MINUS_DST_COLOR = 6 - 1 - destination color

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDFACTOR_SRC_ALPHA = 7 - source alpha

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDFACTOR_ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA = 8 - 1 - source alpha

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDFACTOR_DST_ALPHA = 9 - destination alpha

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDFACTOR_ONE_MINUS_DST_ALPHA = 10 - 1 - destination alpha

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDFACTOR_CONSTANT_COLOR = 11 - blend constant

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDFACTOR_ONE_MINUS_CONSTANT_COLOR = 12 - 1 - blend constant

=item SDL_GPU_BLENDFACTOR_SRC_ALPHA_SATURATE = 13 - min(source alpha, 1 - destination alpha)

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUFilter

Specifies a filter operation used by a sampler.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_FILTER_NEAREST = 0 - Point filtering.

=item SDL_GPU_FILTER_LINEAR = 1 - Linear filtering.

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUSamplerMipmapMode

Specifies a mipmap mode used by a sampler.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_SAMPLERMIPMAPMODE_NEAREST = 0 - Point filtering.

=item SDL_GPU_SAMPLERMIPMAPMODE_LINEAR = 1 - Linear filtering.

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUSamplerAddressMode

Specifies behavior of texture sampling when the coordinates exceed the 0-1 range.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_SAMPLERADDRESSMODE_REPEAT = 0 - Specifies that the coordinates will wrap around.

=item SDL_GPU_SAMPLERADDRESSMODE_MIRRORED_REPEAT = 1 - Specifies that the coordinates will wrap around mirrored.

=item SDL_GPU_SAMPLERADDRESSMODE_CLAMP_TO_EDGE = 2 - Specifies that the coordinates will clamp to the 0-1 range.

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUPresentMode

Specifies the timing that will be used to present swapchain textures to the OS.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_PRESENTMODE_VSYNC = 0

=item SDL_GPU_PRESENTMODE_IMMEDIATE = 1

=item SDL_GPU_PRESENTMODE_MAILBOX = 2

=back

=head2 SDL_GPUSwapchainComposition

Specifies the texture format and colorspace of the swapchain textures.

=over

=item SDL_GPU_SWAPCHAINCOMPOSITION_SDR = 0

=item SDL_GPU_SWAPCHAINCOMPOSITION_SDR_LINEAR = 1

=item SDL_GPU_SWAPCHAINCOMPOSITION_HDR_EXTENDED_LINEAR = 2

=item SDL_GPU_SWAPCHAINCOMPOSITION_HDR10_ST2084 = 3

=back



